commit e14d1e8e0034468ddd1ab3fc1c9983b25d2d8ace
Author: Scout <scout@local>
Date:   Mon Sep 28 00:34:19 2026 -0400

    fix(sse): let a reused session pin outrank OAuth session occupancy
    
    getProviderCredentials ran the OAuth session-occupancy re-pick after
    session affinity. It replaced the connection that
    selectSessionAffinityConnection had chosen with any OAuth peer (priority
    <= selected + 1) that had fewer foreign sessions, and left the pin
    unchanged, so pinned sessions were served off-pin. chat.ts sets
    reserveOAuthSession on its dispatch call, and the same flag drives the
    occupancy reservation, so no setting turned the re-pick off. Issue #8939
    and PR #8940 state that same-session affinity must stay stronger than
    occupancy; PR #5943 gave affinity the same precedence over reset-aware
    re-scoring.
    
    - sessionAffinityPin.ts: the re-pick moves into the affinity leaf as
      pickMoreAvailableOAuthPeer, with the same logic. The fresh-pin path of
      selectSessionAffinityConnection applies it to the LRU pick before it
      writes the pin, with no await between the pin read, that decision and
      the write, so the pin names the account selected for dispatch for
      every non-lease caller. That includes the combo availability check
      (chat.ts:1096-1108): it passes no reserveOAuthSession, and the
      dispatch reuses the pin it writes. The reuse branch and
      planSessionAffinityConnection (lease path) are unchanged.
    - auth.ts: the re-pick is skipped after a non-lease affinity selection.
      This adapts the flag-and-skip of open PR #13102
      (selectedByApiKeyPreference). The re-pick still runs for strategy
      picks, sessionless calls and the lease path. auth.ts neither reads nor
      writes pins, so no second write can replace a newer pin written under
      another selection-mutex key, and no pin can expire between two reads.
      An ineligible pin is not in the pool, so it is not reused and
      occupancy decides the new binding as before.
    
    References:
    - CLIProxyAPI v8.0.2 (4a2c818) sdk/cliproxy/auth/selector.go L1059-1077:
      keep the cached auth when it is available, otherwise bind the
      fallback selector's pick.
    - LiteLLM v1.102.1 (d09bbae)
      litellm/router_utils/pre_call_checks/deployment_affinity_check.py:
      first-writer-wins pin claims, _claim_pin (L344) with the synchronous
      check-and-set of _claim_pin_in_memory (L397), used for the session pin
      at L655. Here each selection makes one read-decide-write.
    - sub2api v0.2.8 (fd80b08)
      backend/internal/service/openai_account_scheduler.go L1323-1330 binds
      the session only after tryAcquireAccountSlot succeeds. That is
      stronger than this patch, which writes the pin at selection, before
      the credentials are materialized and the occupancy is reserved.
    
    Unchanged: the occupancy reservation in materializeConnection and its
    release paths.
    
    Regression test: tests/unit/affinity-outranks-occupancy-8940.test.ts.
    
    (cherry picked from commit 045aa81f30cb9a1fc4f6b426ed940c1956cceda2)

